WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:06.350
Spider-Man: Far From Home is an intense game-changing
movie that clocks in at over two hours long,

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:10.490
but there are still some amazing deleted scenes
cut from the final film as well as a completely

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:12.009
different alternate ending.

00:00:12.009 --> 00:00:17.380
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing 16 deleted scenes,

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:20.610
cancelled characters, and the ending to the
movie you never got to see!

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:24.750
I've got a new Marvel giveaway on this video,
so subscribe, hit the bell and let me know

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.800
what you thought of Far From Home for a chance
to win!

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.150
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care if
you haven't seen it yet.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:35.089
The movie's writers Chris McKenna and Erik
Sommers have revealed there are deleted scenes

00:00:35.089 --> 00:00:39.179
with Happy Hogan where he's "stumbling through
different descriptions" and trying to come

00:00:39.179 --> 00:00:42.129
up with a term of his own for Peter's Spider-Sense.

00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:46.499
In the final film, however, it's Aunt May
who gets to name Peter's special power in

00:00:46.499 --> 00:00:47.499
the MCU.

00:00:47.499 --> 00:00:50.410
"I thought that you could sense that with
your 'Peter Tingle'"

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:54.789
The reason the writers chose Spidey's aunt
to coin that particular phrase was to dial

00:00:54.789 --> 00:00:56.949
up the embarrassment factor for Peter.

00:00:56.949 --> 00:00:58.949
"Do not start calling it my Peter Tingle."

00:00:58.949 --> 00:01:03.629
The worst thing for Pete is that May has also
told Happy and it looks like the term is gonna

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:04.629
stick.

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:06.119
"You get that Peter Tingle back online."

00:01:06.119 --> 00:01:10.600
Before Peter left for his school trip to Europe,
originally he had a long to-do list of things

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.520
that ended up being cut from the final film/movie.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:13.600
"Did you get your passport?"

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.140
"Peter Parker here to pick up a passport please."

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.140
"Yeah."

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.140
"Any toothpaste?"

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:21.210
"Uh huh."

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:22.659
"Take down the Manfredi mob?"

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:23.659
"Yeah I did."

00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:27.570
And there's an awesome extended action scene
of Peter taking down the Manfredi crime syndicate.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:32.540
"You gonna be the next Iron Man, now?"

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:38.450
"Well no, I don't have time, I'm too busy
doing your jobs."

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.450
"Oooh!

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.450
What?!"

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:41.619
"I'm kidding, I'm kidding, look, keep up the
good work!

00:01:41.619 --> 00:01:43.390
Because I am going on vacation!"

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:44.759
"I love that guy."

00:01:44.759 --> 00:01:49.189
This deleted scene is a nice bit of street-level
action and feels similar to how Spidey took

00:01:49.189 --> 00:01:52.299
down the ATM criminals in Spider-Man: Homecoming.

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:57.531
The Manfredi crime family are prominent Spider-Man
villains in the comics and hardcore MCU fans

00:01:57.531 --> 00:02:01.969
may also recall that they appeared in the
second season of Agent Carter where Joseph

00:02:01.969 --> 00:02:06.350
Manfredi was the leader of a bigger crime
syndicate called the Maggia.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.360
Also on the To-Do list that was cut from the
movie was Peter getting the "dual headphone

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:15.080
adaptor" he wanted for watching movies together
with MJ, as well as a European travel plug,

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.080
and toothpaste.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.430
For this he visited Delmar's Store which previously
featured in Homecoming.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:20.430
"Planning a trip?"

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:21.430
"Uh, going to Europe.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.720
It's a school trip."

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.880
Remember in Spidey's first solo film that
Mr Delmar thought Spider-Man was fighting

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.230
the Avengers when he saw him taking on some
masked criminals.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:34.980
In fact, Delmar's bodega was destroyed when
the criminal's tech spun out of control during

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.230
that fight.

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:41.040
After the deli caught fire, Spidey jumped
in to rescue Mr Delmar and his cat Murph.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.940
And you can see that moment referenced in
the deleted scene in the newspaper cuttings

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.290
that are up on the wall.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:50.909
Also chopped from the new movie was Peter
going to collect his passport for his trip

00:02:50.909 --> 00:02:51.909
abroad.

00:02:51.909 --> 00:02:53.440
"Peter Parker here to pick up a passport please."

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.870
That dialogue sounds like the writers were
going for something along the lines of the

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:00.480
well-known tongue-twister 'Peter Piper picked
a peck of pickled peppers'.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.620
Now, you might have noticed that this passport
doesn't have any years on it either for Peter's

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:08.830
year of birth or for the issue or expiration
dates.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:13.209
The years may have simply been removed to
avoid potentially giving away any spoilers

00:03:13.209 --> 00:03:14.209
for Endgame.

00:03:14.209 --> 00:03:19.069
However, Marvel did mess up the timeline in
Spider-Man: Homecoming with an 8-year time

00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:23.849
jump which they had to retcon later when they
released an official timeline for the MCU.

00:03:23.849 --> 00:03:27.480
So, perhaps leaving out the dates is a little
nod to that?

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:31.319
By the way, there's a nice easter egg in the
day and month for Peter's birthday on the

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:32.319
passport.

00:03:32.319 --> 00:03:37.200
The tenth of August 1962 was the date that
Spider-Man debuted in Marvel Comics.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:41.780
Another deleted scene from Peter's trip preparations
saw him selling all of his toys to raise enough

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:45.650
money for the Black Dahlia necklace that he
buys for MJ in Venice.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:49.660
The scene had Peter getting a little emotional
because among the various toys that he was

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:53.920
selling were some vintage Star Wars action
figures that were supposed to have originally

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.620
belonged to Uncle Ben.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:04:00.260
The action figures appeared on the shelf in
Peter's room in Homecoming, and there's one

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:04.400
character, Lobot, which is a favourite of
Marvel Studios chief Kevin Feige, that Peter

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.010
would have ended up keeping.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:10.560
Lobot is Lando Calrissian's administrator
in Cloud City, and although he doesn't get

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:15.100
any speaking lines in Empire Strikes Back,
he does wear a distinctive-looking cybernetic

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:19.410
headpiece which enables him to communicate
with the city's central computer.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:24.260
The irony of this deleted scene is that although,
as we've known since Civil War, Peter Parker

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:28.500
is a Star Wars fan;
"Hey guys, you ever see that really old movie?

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:29.830
Empire Strikes Back?"

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:34.560
Actor Tom Holland has admitted that he's not
really into Star Wars himself and hasn't even

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.979
seen The Empire Strikes Back, so he doesn't
really know who Lobot is.

00:04:38.979 --> 00:04:43.560
By the way, Peter scrabbling to get some money
together to impress MJ with a gift in the

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:48.680
MCU reminds me of how Tobey Maguire's Peter
Parker took part in a wrestling match with

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:53.670
the idea of buying a car to impress Mary Jane
in Sam Raimi's first Spider-Man film.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:58.190
Far From Home's director Jon Watts and Tom
Holland have both said that all these deleted

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:02.210
scenes in New York were cut because the intention
was to get Peter and the other students to

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:04.270
Europe as quickly as possible.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:08.490
These discarded scenes will be appearing as
part of a Marvel One-Shot, a bonus short film

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:11.160
which will be on the movie's Blu-ray release.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:15.690
There's a moment in Far From Home where Nick
Fury tranquilises Ned with a dart in a scene

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:18.890
that calls back to Captain America: The Winter
Soldier.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:23.710
Peter's been dodging Fury's phone calls so
Fury's/he's arrived in person to ask for Spidey's

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:24.710
help.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:28.460
And as they leave the hotel room, there's
an amusing clip that ended up getting cut.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:29.830
"Is he gonna be OK like that?"

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:33.580
"Might wanna turn him over so he doesn't swallow
his tongue."

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:37.949
One location that Peter almost visited with
his classmates on their European tour is New

00:05:37.949 --> 00:05:43.090
Asgard, which is where the surviving Asgardians
settled after the events of Ragnarok, and

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:47.370
where Thor and co were hanging out, playing
video games in Avengers: Endgame.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:51.710
It could have been fun to see Peter Parker
cross paths with Valkyrie, the new Queen of

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:56.810
Asgard, and also check in with Miek and Korg
for an update on Noobmaster69.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:06:01.240
The movie's mid-credits scene was pretty amazing
with the surprise return of J.K. Simmons'

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:06.630
J. Jonah Jameson as a conspiracy theorist
commentator for The Daily Bugle website, offering

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:11.130
up one of his typically prejudiced rants where
he twists the truth about Spider-Man, saying

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:12.260
he's the real villain.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:16.360
Fans have been going crazy for this ending
as it brings back one of the most popular

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:21.500
characters and actors from the Sam Raimi trilogy,
however, originally an alternate ending was

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:26.050
considered that could have brought Anthony
Mackie's new Captain America in for a post-credits

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:28.970
scene or late on in the movie's third act.

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:33.780
In an interview with ComicBook.com, Marvel
Studios' creative executive Eric Carroll said

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:37.800
they discussed bringing in Falcon's Captain
America "at the end, [...] once Peter arced,

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:42.099
and he's sort of [...] leading the team, [...] maybe
he calls in a favour [from Sam Wilson]."

00:06:42.099 --> 00:06:46.960
However, this likely didn't happen because,
as Kevin Feige has said, Far From Home is

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:51.420
ultimately about Peter "getting out of the
shadow, not just of Tony but of the Avengers

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:52.420
in general."

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:54.150
"Are you going to step up or not?"

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:58.430
So although Mackie's Captain America missed
out on debuting in Far From Home, he'll be

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:02.979
taking on Cap's mantle for the first time
in his new Disney+ series "Falcon &amp; The Winter

00:07:02.979 --> 00:07:03.979
Soldier".

00:07:03.979 --> 00:07:08.610
You can learn more about why Steve chose Falcon
to be his successor and discover the future

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.071
of Captain America in my other video.

00:07:10.071 --> 00:07:11.071
There's a card for that here and in the video
description.

00:07:11.071 --> 00:07:14.510
Other characters that could have appeared
in Spider-Man's second solo movie are the

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:16.820
villains Scorpion and the Vulture.

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:21.280
Actor Michael Mando's introduction to the
MCU as Mac Gargan was teased in Homecoming's

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:24.940
mid-credits scene where he tried to find out
Spidey's true identity.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:25.940
"This?

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:27.500
It's not on you.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.710
It's on our little spider friend.

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:32.599
I've got some boys on the outside who would
love to meet him.

00:07:32.599 --> 00:07:36.050
You know, take a picture, slice his throat,
put his head in a dryer.

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:37.759
And I heard a rumor.

00:07:37.759 --> 00:07:39.639
You know who he is."

00:07:39.639 --> 00:07:44.760
When asked by ComicBookMovie.com why Vulture
and Scorpion weren't included in the sequel,

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:48.639
Jon Watts said "We never really found the
right moment to do something like that.

00:07:48.639 --> 00:07:51.690
But […] they're both still out there, and
[…] as we move forward with these films,

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:55.430
we're building out this rich world that we
can continually draw from."

00:07:55.430 --> 00:08:00.979
Indeed, with Spider-Man's identity now exposed
by Mysterio's leaked video, Mac Gargan's Scorpion

00:08:00.979 --> 00:08:05.539
is bound to take a very keen interest in Peter
Parker and he may try to get his friends on

00:08:05.539 --> 00:08:09.240
the outside to target Peter as he already
threatened.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:13.789
Before the film came out, there was also talk
that Norman Osborn might make an appearance,

00:08:13.789 --> 00:08:18.479
with rumours suggesting that he or Oscorp
are the new buyers of the Avengers Tower.

00:08:18.479 --> 00:08:22.930
Although we do see Spidey swing by near the
Avengers Tower, any indication of who may

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:25.169
have bought the building has been cleverly
hidden.

00:08:25.169 --> 00:08:29.820
However, when Jon Watts was asked about Norman
Osborn, he explained that Osborn wasn't considered

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:34.190
for this film in the end, but that he is still
available for a future story.

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:39.050
Jessica Drew, aka Spider-Woman, is another
character that Marvel was reportedly considering

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:42.050
to make her MCU debut in Far From Home.

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:45.690
Apparently, two actresses in particular were
seriously considered for the role.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:50.351
First was Shailene Woodley who played Mary
Jane Watson in The Amazing Spider-Man 2 before

00:08:50.351 --> 00:08:52.180
her character was cut from that movie.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:56.440
And there was also Olivia Cooke who you may
know from Ready Player One.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:09:00.830
Sources for The Hashtag Show suggested that
Jessica Drew was going to be introduced as

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:06.040
a "Bond-girl type international agent" that
Peter would meet on his trip to Europe.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:10.090
Given Spidey's incredible popularity, it's
surprising that there still hasn't been a

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:14.660
live-action incarnation of Spider-Woman, but
hopefully that could change soon.

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:18.710
One character that Jon Watts confirmed was
considered for Spidey's sequel is Captain

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:19.710
Britain.

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:23.920
Clearly, Peter Parker's trip to London would
have been a great opportunity for a potential

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:28.580
cameo, especially after Avengers: Endgame
where Peggy Carter's mention of Braddock hints

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:31.360
at the existence of Captain Britain in the
MCU.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:35.640
However, according to Watts, they just couldn't
come up with a "clever way of incorporating

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:40.000
Captain Britain" into the Far From Home script
and their attempts to do so ended up feeling

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.500
like "shoehorned in reference[s]".

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:47.000
A character that Homecoming neatly set up
for future appearances was Miles Morales.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:51.730
When Donald Glover's The Prowler appeared
in Spidey's first solo MCU movie he mentioned

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:53.030
his nephew, Miles.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:57.700
However, Miles didn't appear in Far From Home
primarily because the character had just had

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:03.330
a high-profile introduction, albeit in animated
form, in Spider-Man: Into The Spider-Verse.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:07.080
Despite this, Jon Watts has said that Miles
could still be introduced in live-action in

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.040
a movie further down the line.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:13.540
By the way, Tom Holland himself had a deleted
cameo as another Peter Parker in Into The

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:14.540
Spider-Verse.

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:19.152
A couple more trailer scenes I spotted which
weren't in the movie include this one of MJ

00:10:19.152 --> 00:10:23.470
and the newly-in-love couple Betty and Ned
passing through customs.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:27.360
And there's an extended scene of Peter's encounter
with the Italian customs officer which was

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.320
trimmed down in the final movie.

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:30.320
"Questo?"

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:31.320
"They're my pyjamas.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:32.520
You know .. pyjamas.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:33.590
They're bigger because..

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:35.170
That's how I like them."

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:38.060
"Pyjamas, OK, that's fine."

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:41.980
And when Hydro-Man emerges from the Venice
canals to wreak destruction [on the city],

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:45.870
it looks like this shot of Peter perched on
the roof of a Venetian bridge was chopped

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:46.870
from the film.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:51.180
The shot in the actual movie has Peter in
a different position and wearing a [purple]

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:52.180
carnival mask.

00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:56.440
So, what do you think about any of these deleted
scenes and do you wish any had been included

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:57.440
in the movie?

